    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:22e6c012542452b4",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "652e5a8d63d1031a367009a298c23e2608ae20f8d4a5a5e6edecc32de6f82cb5",
      "text": "We head towards the Peruvian border, where Lake Titicaca lies. On the way, we visit the imposing ruins of Tiwanaku (1,580 +1,000 CE), the remains of one of South America's oldest civilisations. You'll see the Gate of the Sun, the Kalasasaya Temple and the pyramids, monuments to the achievements of the Tiwanaku culture. The Tiwanaku people were skilled in agriculture, water engineering, architecture and medicine, and had a sophisticated social organisation. Natural upheavals, including prolonged droughts, led to the civilisation's collapse at the end of the first millennium CE, after which it mysteriously disappeared. The excursion ends in the border town of Desaguadero, where you'll transfer to your hotel in Puno.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6kxp21-vlap279rsy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:eb387400a92b4c0f",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "814caf77307cdfb09151d2baccc8eff773ff06acd1ba4be35c5b7f37c951cbf9",
      "text": "In the afternoon, visit the Uros Islands with an English-speaking guide. The islands are built from reeds and are home to Indigenous Aymara people who have preserved their traditional way of life, customs, beliefs and dress.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6kxp21-vlap279rsy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
